# Conformance probe pack for gate blocks inside kinds (spec 0.17, ruling 1).
# Fixed `bits` layout, least significant bit first. Public. One byte per
# word. Exercises: a block is evaluated after its kind is selected, so a kind
# whose block does not hold is still selected; `requires` sees the entity
# only; a `when` written on a block's gate bits defeats that block, so its
# key cannot be encoded.
#
#   byte 0       w, common
#   byte 1       bits 8-11: the kind (1: a, 2: b); bit 12: x (a) or z (b) is
#                valid
#   byte 2       x (a); y (b), when bits 8-11 are 3, which kind b never has
#   byte 3       z (b)
format     conformance-gates-kinds
version    0.17.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
field    probe.w   0:0:8    uint
kind     a
when     0:8:4   1
requires probe.x
if       0:12:1  1
  field  probe.x   0:16:8   uint
end
kind     b
when     0:8:4   2
if       0:8:4   3
  field  probe.y   0:16:8   uint
end
if       0:12:1  1
  field  probe.z   0:24:8   uint
end
